<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine monthly oilseed crushings.</title>
<headline>Argentine monthly oilseed crushings.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine mills crushed 1,523,763 tonnes of oilseed in November 1996 against 1,291,202 tonnes in November 1995, the Agriculture Secretariat said.</p>
<p>(Breakdown in tonnes, year-earlier in brackets).</p>
<p> Soybean	     1,039,995    (970,756)</p>
<p> Sunflowerseed	 365,813    (297,620)</p>
<p> Linseed		   8,781	(3,322)</p>
<p> Groundnutseed	  21,197     (19,504)</p>
<p> Cottonseed		  nil	  (nil)</p>
<p>Output in November was as follows:</p>
<p> ..............Oils...................Meals</p>
<p> Soybean     184,894    (173,332)    824,505     (789,240)</p>
<p> Sunflower   151,164    (117,704)    151,582     (119,692)</p>
<p> Linseed	   218	(1,103)	  nil	   (nil)</p>
<p> Groundnut     8,123	(7,475)     12,107	(11,239)</p>
<p> Cottonseed	nil	  (nil)	  nil	   (nil)</p>
<p> .......................Expellers</p>
<p> Soybean    3,638   (3,168)  Groundnut   nil	  (nil)</p>
<p> Sunflower    nil     (nil)  Cottonseed  nil	  (nil)</p>
<p> Linseed	557   (2,057)</p>
<p>Crushings from January to November, with the same period in 1995 in brackets, were:</p>
<p> Soybean	     9,626,830    (8,247,952)</p>
<p> Sunflowerseed     4,783,581    (4,581,196)</p>
<p> Linseed		 128,351	(107,809)</p>
<p> Groundnutseed	 143,589	(115,643)</p>
<p> Cottonseed	    432,947	(419,616)</p>
<p>Output in January through November (1995 in brackets):</p>
<p> ..............Oils...................Meals</p>
<p> Soybean   1,708,482  (1,426,016)  7,696,808  (6,549,929)</p>
<p>Sunflower 1,926,907  (1,832,820)  2,012,158  (1,952,259)</p>
<p> Linseed	38,923     (36,996)	  nil	  (nil)</p>
<p> Groundnut    55,495     (44,833)     82,514     (65,339)</p>
<p> Cottonseed   66,659     (64,902)    205,507    (194,791)</p>
<p> .......................Expellers</p>
<p> Soybean    32,292 (50,054)   Groundnut   nil	  (nil)</p>
<p> Sunflower   6,419  (4,234)   Cottonseed  nil	  (nil)</p>
<p> Linseed    80,419 (74,363)</p>
<p>((-- Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655))</p>
